# Cloudflare Pages redirects — client-side app & auth routes only.
#
# The public marketing pages are pre-rendered to static HTML (dist/<route>/index.html)
# and are served directly by Cloudflare, so they must NOT be caught by a catch-all.
# A top-level 404.html is present, which makes Cloudflare serve a real HTTP 404
# for any unmatched path (no soft-404 to the homepage).

# ── Client-rendered routes → SPA shell (hard navigation / refresh) ──
/app               /index.html   200
/app/*             /index.html   200
/login             /index.html   200
/signup            /index.html   200
/verify-email      /index.html   200
/workspace         /index.html   200
/workspace/*       /index.html   200
/upgrade-business  /index.html   200
/admin             /index.html   200
/admin/*           /index.html   200
